<p><strong>Capacitance.</strong> Nobody puts capacitors on the wordline on purpose. They are <em>parasitic</em>: they come with the transistors the wordline drives and with the wire itself. To read or write a row, the decoder drives that row's wordline from 0 V to VDD. This turns on the access transistors in every cell of the row, which connects each cell to its bitlines:</p>
